      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "This is a pure mathematics/ML hypothesis test (bootstrap solution-space rigidity). I will design a minimal numerical experiment: (1) generate simple target functions (polynomial, sin) with w constraints; (2) train small fully-connected nets of varying hidden width N to fit those w points; (3) evaluate on a held-out set of points; (4) record N_c(w) as the minimum width achieving max absolute error ≤ 1e-3 on holdouts; (5) sweep w and fit scaling (constant vs power law vs log). The experiment will be implemented in Python using PyTorch (or numpy+scipy for small nets), with deterministic initialization and multiple random seeds for reliability. I will then produce a report with N_c(w) values, plots, and conclusion on rigidity."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "skill",
      "value": "None (custom ML experiment)"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "For polynomial targets, N_c(w) should saturate at a small constant once w exceeds the polynomial degree (rigid behavior). For sin (analytic but not polynomial), N_c(w) may grow slowly (sublinear) as w increases, reflecting the need to resolve oscillatory features. The scaling will be discriminable: constant plateau vs increasing trend."
    },
